.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rev-stealth-spider 1  "rev-stealth-spider " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-spider \- AUP\-gated browse + optional CF eval + optional adaptive relocate
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth spider\fR [\fB\-\-output\-format\fR] <\fB\-\-url\fR> [\fB\-\-session\-id\fR] [\fB\-\-mobile\-preset\fR] [\fB\-\-cf\-evaluate\fR] [\fB\-\-vpn\fR] [\fB\-\-stable\-id\fR] [\fB\-\-threshold\fR] [\fB\-\-strict\fR] [\fB\-\-i\-have\-authorization\fR] [\fB\-\-obscura\fR] [\fB\-\-parse\-store\fR] [\fB\-\-use\-auth\fR] [\fB\-\-auth\-domain\fR] [\fB\-\-http\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-auto\-fallback\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-auto\-fallback\fR] [\fB\-\-dump\-html\fR] [\fB\-\-wait\-ms\fR] [\fB\-\-wait\-selector\fR] [\fB\-\-require\-vpn\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-no\-vpn\fR] [\fB\-\-vpn\-instance\fR] [\fB\-\-proxy\-tier\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-fallback\fR] [\fB\-\-leak\-poll\-secs\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-cache\fR] [\fB\-\-cache\-refresh\fR] [\fB\-\-cache\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-cache\-ttl\fR] [\fB\-\-recipe\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-recipe\-endpoint\fR] [\fB\-\-recipe\-param\fR] [\fB\-\-recipe\-no\-learn\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
AUP\-gated browser fetch with optional Cloudflare Turnstile evaluation and adaptive element relocation. Honours the layered config / recipe cache; falls back from obscura to reqwest unless \-\-no\-auto\-fallback is set. Replays stored auth cookies via \-\-use\-auth. AUTHORIZED TARGETS ONLY.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-output\-format\fR \fI<OUTPUT_FORMAT>\fR
Output format for this subcommand: `human` (default) or `json`. Shadows the global `\-\-format` for this invocation. Same value enum as the global flag; the JSON output is documented under `docs/json\-schemas/cli/<subcommand>.output.json`
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR
Target URL
.TP
\fB\-\-session\-id\fR \fI<SESSION_ID>\fR
Session id (auto\-generated when omitted)
.TP
\fB\-\-mobile\-preset\fR \fI<MOBILE_PRESET>\fR
Mobile fingerprint preset slug
.TP
\fB\-\-cf\-evaluate\fR
Evaluate Cloudflare Turnstile resilience (defender\-testbed; no solver)
.TP
\fB\-\-vpn\fR
Route through `vpn\-rotate` before launch
.TP
\fB\-\-stable\-id\fR \fI<STABLE_ID>\fR
stable_id to locate via `stealth\-parse` after navigation
.TP
\fB\-\-threshold\fR \fI<THRESHOLD>\fR [default: 0.85]
Similarity threshold for relocate
.TP
\fB\-\-strict\fR
Treat Ambiguous relocate as a hard failure (exit code 10)
.TP
\fB\-\-i\-have\-authorization\fR
AUP bypass (logs a warn). Equivalent to env\-ack for the day
.TP
\fB\-\-obscura\fR \fI<OBSCURA>\fR
Path to the obscura binary. Overridable via env
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBREV_STEALTH_OBSCURA\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-parse\-store\fR \fI<PARSE_STORE>\fR
Optional ParseStore path (defaults to `~/.rev_scraping/parse.sqlite`)
.TP
\fB\-\-use\-auth\fR \fI<USE_AUTH>\fR
Replay stored auth cookies and browser headers from the named profile
.TP
\fB\-\-auth\-domain\fR \fI<AUTH_DOMAIN>\fR
Auth AAD/domain context to load; defaults to the target host
.TP
\fB\-\-http\-only\fR
Skip obscura entirely and fetch via reqwest. Implies no JS execution, no CF eval, no DOM injection
.TP
\fB\-\-auto\-fallback\fR
When obscura launch / CDP fails, automatically retry with reqwest. Default true; set `\-\-no\-auto\-fallback` to disable for deterministic agent workflows that need a hard exit\-3 on browser failure
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-auto\-fallback\fR
Explicit disable for `\-\-auto\-fallback` (overrides the default)
.TP
\fB\-\-dump\-html\fR \fI<DUMP_HTML>\fR
Dump the fetched HTML to the given path (UTF\-8). With obscura, the post\-render `document.documentElement.outerHTML` is captured (so SPAs land hydrated); with the reqwest fallback / `\-\-http\-only`, the raw response body is written. Parent directories are created as needed and the file is created with mode `0600` on Unix
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\-ms\fR \fI<WAIT_MS>\fR
After obscura navigate completes, wait N milliseconds before dumping the HTML. Useful for SPA hydration. No\-op on the reqwest fallback path
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\-selector\fR \fI<WAIT_SELECTOR>\fR
After obscura navigate completes, wait until the given CSS selector appears in the DOM (max 30 seconds). Takes precedence over `\-\-wait\-ms`. No\-op on the reqwest fallback path
.TP
\fB\-\-require\-vpn\fR
Force the VPN\-required guard ON for this invocation. Wins over `policy.toml`. Loses to env `REV_SCRAPING_REQUIRE_VPN=1` only in the sense that env can\*(Aqt be loosened further
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-no\-vpn\fR
Allow this invocation to proceed without a VPN. Loses to env `REV_SCRAPING_REQUIRE_VPN=1` (which is the only way to enforce the policy from outside the process)
.TP
\fB\-\-vpn\-instance\fR \fI<VPN_INSTANCE>\fR
Force this invocation to use the named VPN instance, overriding the HRW session\-sticky pick. Useful for tests and reproducible runs. Must match a `name` in the configured `vpn_instances` list
.TP
\fB\-\-proxy\-tier\fR \fI<PROXY_TIER>\fR
Force a named proxy tier (e.g. "direct", "surfshark", "warp", "iproyal") or "auto" to use the configured fallback chain. Mutually exclusive with `\-\-vpn\-instance` unless the tier is exactly "surfshark"
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-fallback\fR
Disable the fallback chain; one attempt at the selected tier only
.TP
\fB\-\-leak\-poll\-secs\fR \fI<LEAK_POLL_SECS>\fR [default: 30]
Polling interval (seconds) for the background leak monitor. Only honoured when `require_vpn=true`. Range [5, 300]; out\-of\-range values are clamped. Default 30s
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-cache\fR
Skip recipe lookup AND skeleton save for this invocation
.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-refresh\fR
Ignore any existing recipe, run full discovery, and overwrite the recipe on success
.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-only\fR
Hard\-require a recipe hit. On miss, exit code 9 and do nothing
.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-ttl\fR \fI<CACHE_TTL>\fR [default: 30]
Treat recipes whose `last_verified` is older than DAYS as expired. Default: 30 days. Expired recipes are refreshed and overwritten
.TP
\fB\-\-recipe\-dir\fR \fI<RECIPE_DIR>\fR
Override the recipe directory (defaults to `~/.rev_scraping/sites/`)
.TP
\fB\-\-recipe\-endpoint\fR \fI<RECIPE_ENDPOINT>\fR
When a recipe is hit and exposes API endpoints, call the endpoint matching this `purpose` directly via reqwest, skipping browser entirely
.TP
\fB\-\-recipe\-param\fR \fI<KEY=VALUE>\fR
Placeholder substitutions for the recipe endpoint URL. Repeatable; e.g. `\-\-recipe\-param username=alice \-\-recipe\-param id=42`
.TP
\fB\-\-recipe\-no\-learn\fR
Disable Phase 7c auto\-learning (Network capture + JS bundle scan + recipe upsert). Privacy\-sensitive runs may opt out; the skeleton save still applies unless `\-\-no\-cache` is set. Default: off (i.e. learning is ON)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth spider \-\-url https://example.com \-\-i\-have\-authorization
  $ rev\-stealth spider \-\-url https://x.test \-\-use\-auth my\-profile \-\-require\-vpn
  $ rev\-stealth spider \-\-url https://x.test \-\-http\-only \-\-dump\-html out.html

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Fetch + (optional) relocate succeeded.
  1  UserError        Bad args / AUP rejection / config validation failure.
  2  TransientError   Network / obscura / VPN flap (retryable).
  3  PermanentError   Permanent fetch failure or unsupported config.
  4  AuthExpired      Stored auth profile missing/expired (Phase 9a).
  7  Leak             Leak detected (fail\-closed when \-\-require\-vpn).

ENV:
  REV_STEALTH_OBSCURA       Override the obscura binary path.
  REV_SCRAPING_HOME         Override `~/.rev_scraping/` base.
  REV_SCRAPING_REQUIRE_VPN  When `1`, enforces VPN\-required guard.
